    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Undhiyu"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " takes its name from cooking upside down in a clay pot: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "undhiyu term ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "undhiyu-term"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Small savoury dumplings called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "methi muthia",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "methi-muthia"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " are buried among the vegetables. The traditional bean is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "surti papdi ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "surti-papdi"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "; green beans are used here."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The coconut and herb paste is the flavour core of the dish. Grind it finely and make sure every vegetable is coated before sealing the pot."
          }
        ]
      },
